  "description_text": "Part of a collection of five contemporary homes designed and developed by Alloy, 171 Water Street is an 18-foot-wide townhouse with four bedrooms, three baths, two private outdoor spaces and a dedicated garage parking space accessible directly from the house. . Each townhouse in the collection sits on its own lot. The main level brings the kitchen, dining, and living areas together. The living room has a 20-foot ceiling, tall windows, and a fireplace. A terrace off the dining area provides space for outdoor dining, and the finished mezzanine overlooks the living room. The primary suite occupies its own floor and includes a fireplace, a walk-in dressing area, and a bath with dual sinks, a separate shower, and a freestanding tub. Two bedrooms share a full bath on the upper level, while a fourth bedroom and full bath are on the entry level. The owners replaced the HVAC system in full, built out the mezzanine, and installed Deltalight GYN fixtures throughout, adding lighting in several areas. The private roof terrace features TimberTech Vintage Collection decking and views toward the Manhattan Bridge. Brooklyn Bridge Park, the waterfront, and DUMBO's restaurants and shops are nearby.",
